{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFpZRqWKUNu3YghZZjec","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`report.metais` is a DORA major ICT-incident report template (Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/302). It's a package for the `metais` tool, which is installed here. It needs three input files in a data directory: `stage`, `entity` and `incident`. The package renders them into `incident-report.md`.\n\n**1. `stage`** (field 1.1) is one of `\"initial notification\"`, `\"intermediate report\"` or `\"final report\"`. The stage decides which fields are mandatory.\n\n**2. `entity`** is section 1, with these fields:\n- Submitting entity name and code (LEI).\n- Affected entity types.\n- Primary and second contact: name, email and telephone.\n- Reporting currency, for example `EUR`.\n- Parent undertaking name and LEI, if the entity is part of a group.\n- The affected entity's name and LEI (1.5 and 1.6), if it isn't the entity submitting the report.\n\n**3. `incident`** is sections 2 to 4, and how much you fill in depends on the stage:\n- **Initial notification:** section 2 only. That means:\n  - reference code, which never changes after the first report;\n  - detection and classification timestamps;\n  - a description;\n  - the classification criteria;\n  - how the incident was discovered;\n  - whether the business continuity plan was activated;\n  - countries affected, if geographical spread is among the criteria.\n- **Intermediate report:** everything above plus the mandatory section 3 fields.\n- **Final report:** everything above plus the mandatory section 4 fields.\n\nSome fields become mandatory only when others are given or apply. For example, 3.3 is required once 3.16 (the service downtime) is given, and 3.34 once 3.33 is true. The full list is in `inputs/incident.md`. A few conditions, such as 2.8 for a third-party provider origin, can't be detected from the data. You have to judge whether they apply.\n\nFormats:\n- **Dates and times:** UTC, written `2026-03-02T06:40:00Z`.\n- **Durations:** `DD:HH:MM`.\n- **Percentages:** numbers from 0 to 100.\n- **Files:** `.json`, `.yaml` or `.yml`.\n\nKeep one data directory per incident. For each later report, change `stage`, add that stage's fields and correct anything that has changed. Then run:\n\n```\nmetais validate report.metais --data <dir>\nmetais render report.metais --data <dir> --out <new-dir>\n```\n\n`validate` lists every missing mandatory field and every badly typed value in one pass. The package only renders the report. You still have to file it with your competent authority through the channel it prescribes.\n\nThe package has worked examples for all three stages. Run `metais ls report.metais examples/initial/ -r` to list the initial one. Its inputs are a good starting template.\n\nIf you give me the incident details, I can build the data directory and run validate and render."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":634,"cache_read_input_tokens":29042,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":634,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9586cae9-4840-4bd0-bbc4-09ffe3f83890","uuid":"f54d2659-1219-4cff-9849-a8ca48f25e1d","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:02:00.743Z","request_id":"req_011CgFpZQi2bPhX6PrwTXWea"}
